ion being reality well this idea  isn't exactly a gear six per se but i  think of it more as a final point for  gear 5 not a new form in itself but the  full actualization of the current form  and most importantly this brings themes  of imagination full circle into the core  theme of the entire show that of course  being dreams the idea at the basis of  one piece is to follow your dreams no  matter how crazy or ridiculous they are  and a seeming requirement for being a  straw hat has always been that you need  to have one of those crazy dreams not  just the straw hats though these slaves  of the world nobles wish that they could  be free just as nika had freed them in  the past the people of fishman island  wish to be able to live as equals under  the sun and so on and so on and i think  that this will be the ultimate  quote-unquote power of gear 5. it won't  be that luffy is limited only by his  imagination it will be that luffy will  allow the dreams of those around him to  be unlimited by reality in essence luffy  will become a man who can make the  dreams of those around him come true and  again this is more of a symbolic  actualization than a true new form but i  do think that it's something cool that  fits into the themes of the story yet  another possible direction that gear 6  could take us in is leaning into the sun  god aspect of sun god nika there has  been a lot of debate about how much the  original joy boy who was almost  certainly the previous owner of the nika  devil fruit is influencing the actions  and decisions of luffy after his devil  fruit awakening all the laughing and joy  that gear 5 luffy exhibits during fights  suggests that joyboy's will may be  having an effect on him but i think that  we'd all agree that overall luffy is  still luffy his personality his goals  and his dreams have not changed because  of his devil fruit awakening but what if  gear 6 takes luffy's transformation to a  whole other level and instead of just  being a man cal